          "attribute": "question/problem",
          "value": "Consider the vector field $F(x,y,z)=\u27e8x,\\,y,\\,2z\u27e9$ and the surface $S$ defined in Cartesian coordinates as $z=2x+3y$ for $0\\le x\\le 1$ and $0\\le y\\le 1.$ Calculate the flux of $F$ through $S$ with respect to the upward-pointing unit normal vector $n.$\n\n*Hint: You're given that the fundamental vector product of $S$ with respect to its canonical parametrization is $||{r}_{x}\\times {r}_{y}||=\\sqrt{14}.$*",
